  "notes": "pc-r009: Compute-starve sweep, R=4 point \u2014 n_recursions=4 (inner latent-recursion depth per outer supervision step). arm='absolute', seed=42, data_seed=42 held fixed (the established absolute/s42 config). SINGLE variable = n_recursions. The R=8 anchor is on record: 100% at K=2/3/4 with the answer already in y at outer step 0 \u2014 8 inner z-updates per outer step are ample compute to front-load all 4 hops into one outer step, so at R=8 the outer loop carries no hop-clock semantics. NOTE: n_cycles is inert (stored but never read by TinyRecursiveModel.forward); the true recurrence-depth knob is n_recursions. Test: hold n_supervision=8 and shrink n_recursions (R=4 here; R=2 and R=1 in subsequent runs). Genuine iteration (outer loop as a hop clock) => the correct K=4 answer still emerges, at a possibly-later outer step; front-loaded shallow compute => final K=4 acc degrades and/or emergence slides past the available steps as R drops. Everything else identical to the R=8 anchor config (bf16, every-step probe, concat encoder, 100k train, dim=256, n_supervision=8). Questions: (1) At which outer step does y first reach 1.0 at R=4? (2) Does z_probe_acc still saturate the composition chain under starved compute? (3) Does final K=4 acc hold?",
